{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-23156","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23664","text":"The Three-Protocol Stack: [&], PULSE, PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-23157","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23665","text":"This document explains how the three [&] ecosystem protocols compose into a complete substrate for accountable, evolvable, benchmarkable agent systems."}]},{"id":"blk-23158","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  PRISM    — measures loops over time      (diagnostic)   │ OS-009\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  PULSE    — declares loops + circulation   (temporal)    │ OS-010\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  [&]      — composes capabilities          (structural)  │ AmpersandBoxDesign\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"},{"id":"blk-23159","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23666","text":"What each layer answers"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23161","spans":[{"id":"spn-23667","text":"Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-23162","spans":[{"id":"spn-23668","text":"Question"}]},{"id":"blk-23163","spans":[{"id":"spn-23669","text":"Artifact"}]}],"id":"blk-23160","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23164","spans":[{"id":"spn-23670","text":"[[&]](../../AmpersandBoxDesign/docs/index.md)"}]},{"id":"blk-23165","spans":[{"id":"spn-23671","text":"What can each agent do, and how do they compose?"}]},{"id":"blk-23166","spans":[{"id":"spn-23672","marks":["code"],"text":"*.ampersand.json"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23167","spans":[{"id":"spn-23673","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-010-PULSE-SPECIFICATION.md"}],"text":"PULSE"}]},{"id":"blk-23168","spans":[{"id":"spn-23674","text":"How do their processes cycle and signal each other?"}]},{"id":"blk-23169","spans":[{"id":"spn-23675","marks":["code"],"text":"*.pulse.json"},{"id":"spn-23676","text":" (loop manifest)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23170","spans":[{"id":"spn-23677","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-009-PRISM-SPECIFICATION.md"}],"text":"PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-23171","spans":[{"id":"spn-23678","text":"How well do those cycles actually work over time?"}]},{"id":"blk-23172","spans":[{"id":"spn-23679","text":"Diagnostic reports + leaderboards"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23173","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23680","text":"A customer adopting all three writes (at minimum) two files:"}]},{"id":"blk-23174","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"acme-insurance/\n├── acme.ampersand.json   # [&] — capability declarations\n└── acme.pulse.json       # PULSE — loop topology + cadence + connections"},{"id":"blk-23175","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23681","text":"PRISM does not require a separate file — it reads the PULSE manifest directly to discover phases, signatures, and substrates."}]},{"id":"blk-23176","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23682","text":"Three closed loops, three nesting levels"}]},{"id":"blk-23177","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23683","text":"The reference [&] ecosystem already operates with three nested loops:"}]},{"id":"blk-23178","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"PRISM (outer)        compose → interact → observe → reflect → diagnose\n  │\n  └─ Graphonomous    retrieve → route → act → learn → consolidate\n       │\n       └─ Deliberation    survey → triage → dispatch → act → learn"},{"id":"blk-23179","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23684","text":"PULSE encodes this nesting in the "},{"id":"spn-23685","marks":["code"],"text":"nesting"},{"id":"spn-23686","text":" block of each manifest:"}]},{"id":"blk-23180","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23182","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23687","marks":["code"],"text":"prism.benchmark"},{"id":"spn-23688","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-23689","marks":["code"],"text":"inner_loops: [graphonomous.continual_learning]"}]}],"id":"blk-23181","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23184","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23690","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous.continual_learning"},{"id":"spn-23691","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-23692","marks":["code"],"text":"inner_loops: [graphonomous.deliberate]"}]}],"id":"blk-23183","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23186","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23693","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous.deliberate"},{"id":"spn-23694","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-23695","marks":["code"],"text":"parent_loop: graphonomous.continual_learning"}]}],"id":"blk-23185","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-23187","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23696","text":"OS-008 (Agent Harness, draft) is expected to add a fourth outer layer. PULSE supports unbounded nesting depth — adding OS-008 is just another manifest with "},{"id":"spn-23697","marks":["code"],"text":"inner_loops: [prism.benchmark]"},{"id":"spn-23698","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-23188","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23699","text":"How signals flow"}]},{"id":"blk-23189","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23700","text":"Cross-loop signals carry one of five canonical tokens through CloudEvents-compatible envelopes:"}]},{"id":"blk-23190","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"                              ┌────────────────────┐\n                              │  ReputationUpdate  │ ────────────────┐\n                              └────────────────────┘                  │\n                                       ▲                              ▼\n                                       │                    ┌──────────────────┐\n                              ┌────────┴────────┐           │ fleetprompt.trust │\n                              │ OutcomeSignal   │           │  (marketplace)    │\n                              └────────┬────────┘           └──────────────────┘\n                                       │\n        ┌──────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┐\n        │                              │                            │\n        ▼                              ▼                            ▼\n┌──────────────┐            ┌──────────────────┐         ┌────────────────────┐\n│ graphonomous │ ──signal──▶│  prism.benchmark │         │ agentromatic.delib │\n│ (memory loop)│            │ (eval loop)      │         │ (consensus loop)   │\n└──────┬───────┘            └────────┬─────────┘         └─────────┬──────────┘\n       │                             │                              │\n       │ TopologyContext             │ DeliberationResult           │\n       ▼                             ▼                              ▼\n┌──────────────┐            ┌──────────────────┐         ┌────────────────────┐\n│ ConsolidationEvent          (read by other loops as substrate state)        │\n└──────────────┘            └──────────────────┘         └────────────────────┘"},{"id":"blk-23191","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23701","text":"The five tokens are stable for v0.1:"}]},{"id":"blk-23192","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23194","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23702","marks":["code"],"text":"TopologyContext"},{"id":"spn-23703","text":" — emitted by "},{"id":"spn-23704","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-23705","text":", consumed by "},{"id":"spn-23706","marks":["code"],"text":"route"}]}],"id":"blk-23193","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23196","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23707","marks":["code"],"text":"DeliberationResult"},{"id":"spn-23708","text":" — emitted by inner deliberation loops"}]}],"id":"blk-23195","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23198","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23709","marks":["code"],"text":"OutcomeSignal"},{"id":"spn-23710","text":" — emitted by "},{"id":"spn-23711","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-23712","text":" after action results"}]}],"id":"blk-23197","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23200","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23713","marks":["code"],"text":"ReputationUpdate"},{"id":"spn-23714","text":" — canonical reputation/confidence delta"}]}],"id":"blk-23199","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23202","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23715","marks":["code"],"text":"ConsolidationEvent"},{"id":"spn-23716","text":" — emitted by "},{"id":"spn-23717","marks":["code"],"text":"consolidate"},{"id":"spn-23718","text":" phases"}]}],"id":"blk-23201","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-23203","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23719","text":"Conformance composition"}]},{"id":"blk-23204","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23720","text":"A loop is "},{"id":"spn-23721","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE-conforming"},{"id":"spn-23722","text":" if its manifest validates against "},{"id":"spn-23723","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-loop-manifest.v0.1.json"},{"id":"spn-23724","text":" and its runtime passes all 12 conformance tests."}]},{"id":"blk-23205","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23725","text":"A system is "},{"id":"spn-23726","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM-evaluable"},{"id":"spn-23727","text":" automatically once it is PULSE-conforming — PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-23728","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-23729","text":" phase reads the manifest, injects scenarios at the declared "},{"id":"spn-23730","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-23731","text":" boundary, and observes outcomes via the declared "},{"id":"spn-23732","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-23733","text":" phase."}]},{"id":"blk-23206","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23734","text":"A system is "},{"id":"spn-23735","marks":["bold"],"text":"[&]-composable"},{"id":"spn-23736","text":" if its agents declare capabilities with matching "},{"id":"spn-23737","marks":["code"],"text":"accepts_from"},{"id":"spn-23738","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-23739","marks":["code"],"text":"feeds_into"},{"id":"spn-23740","text":" contracts."}]},{"id":"blk-23207","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23741","text":"The three layers are independent. A system may adopt one without the others. Adoption order is typically:"}]},{"id":"blk-23208","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23210","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23742","marks":["bold"],"text":"[&]"},{"id":"spn-23743","text":" (capability declarations) — earliest, lowest commitment"}]}],"id":"blk-23209","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23212","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23744","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE"},{"id":"spn-23745","text":" (loop manifest) — when the system has closed feedback"}]}],"id":"blk-23211","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23214","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23746","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM"},{"id":"spn-23747","text":" (benchmarking) — when the loop is ready to be measured"}]}],"id":"blk-23213","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-23215","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23748","text":"Why three protocols, not one"}]},{"id":"blk-23216","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23749","text":"A monolithic protocol covering capabilities, loops, and benchmarking would be larger, harder to evolve, and harder to adopt incrementally. The three-layer split mirrors how HTTP, HTML, and CSS became ubiquitous separately before converging in the browser."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23218","spans":[{"id":"spn-23750","text":"Concern"}]},{"id":"blk-23219","spans":[{"id":"spn-23751","text":"Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-23220","spans":[{"id":"spn-23752","text":"Cadence of change"}]}],"id":"blk-23217","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23221","spans":[{"id":"spn-23753","text":"What can be done"}]},{"id":"blk-23222","spans":[{"id":"spn-23754","text":"[&]"}]},{"id":"blk-23223","spans":[{"id":"spn-23755","text":"months–years"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23224","spans":[{"id":"spn-23756","text":"How it cycles"}]},{"id":"blk-23225","spans":[{"id":"spn-23757","text":"PULSE"}]},{"id":"blk-23226","spans":[{"id":"spn-23758","text":"weeks–months"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23227","spans":[{"id":"spn-23759","text":"How well it works"}]},{"id":"blk-23228","spans":[{"id":"spn-23760","text":"PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-23229","spans":[{"id":"spn-23761","text":"continuous"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23230","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23762","text":"Different rates of change deserve different protocols."}]},{"id":"blk-23231","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23763","text":"Related"}]},{"id":"blk-23232","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23234","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23764","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/ECOSYSTEM.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem overview"},{"id":"spn-23765","text":" — how every product fits the stack"}]}],"id":"blk-23233","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23236","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23766","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/STACK_COMPLETION.md"}],"text":"Stack status"},{"id":"spn-23767","text":" — versions, test counts, deployment state"}]}],"id":"blk-23235","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23238","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23768","text":"[[&] Protocol docs](../../AmpersandBoxDesign/docs/index.md) — capability composition (structural)"}]}],"id":"blk-23237","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23240","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23769","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-010-PULSE-SPECIFICATION.md"}],"text":"OS-010 PULSE specification"},{"id":"spn-23770","text":" — loop + circulation algebra (temporal)"}]}],"id":"blk-23239","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23242","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23771","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-009-PRISM-SPECIFICATION.md"}],"text":"OS-009 PRISM specification"},{"id":"spn-23772","text":" — cross-system benchmark (diagnostic)"}]}],"id":"blk-23241","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23244","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23773","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/graphonomous/docs/spec/README.md"}],"text":"Graphonomous spec"},{"id":"spn-23774","text":" — the reference memory loop these protocols compose around"}]}],"id":"blk-23243","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-23245","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23775","text":"PULSE implementation docs"}]},{"id":"blk-23246","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23248","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23776","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/ARITHMETIC_INTEGRATION.md"}],"text":"Arithmetic Integration"},{"id":"spn-23777","text":" — how PULSE phases gate on the box-and-box kernel verdict"}]}],"id":"blk-23247","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23250","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23778","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/V0.2-BEHAVIORAL-TYPES.md"}],"text":"V0.2 Behavioral Types"},{"id":"spn-23779","text":" — session-typed phase contracts (draft)"}]}],"id":"blk-23249","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23252","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23780","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/V0.2-IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md"}],"text":"V0.2 Implementation Plan"},{"id":"spn-23781","text":" — roadmap for the v0.2 manifest schema"}]}],"id":"blk-23251","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23254","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23782","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/NPM_PACKAGE.md"}],"text":"NPM Package"},{"id":"spn-23783","text":" — the PULSE validator/conformance package"}]}],"id":"blk-23253","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierak4kalhobp6ousbiv2xqovyuk5kkpa7wooke37qvv3nhm4gw4ouga","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}